  "verifiedRenderBehaviorPerProvider": {
    "xai": "No speed param on the TTS request at all (services/tts-service.cjs generateXai) — every render is at natural/1x pace regardless of any configured speed. Trusted as a canonical 1x source.",
    "elevenlabs": "`speed` is destructured from config in generateElevenLabs but never placed into the request body — the configured speed is silently ignored. Every render is at ElevenLabs' fixed pace (1x-equivalent, not user-adjustable). Trusted as a canonical 1x source.",
    "azure": "BAKES speed into the SSML <prosody rate=\"...\"> tag (services/tts-service.cjs generateAzure, ~line 148-154) — a clip rendered with a non-1.0 configured speed has that pace PHYSICALLY baked into the stored MP3. course_audio has NO persisted per-row speed, so a historical Azure row cannot be verified 1x after the fact. NOT trusted as a canonical copy source (services/shared/clone-copy-match.cjs isTrusted1xEngine excludes it) until proven otherwise."
  },
  "voiceConfigSpeedReadSites": [
    "services/phases/phase8-audio-v13.cjs getSpeedForRole()/getEffectiveSpeed-equivalent (~line 1364, ~line 3996): reads voice_config.voices[role].settings.speed and passes it into the TTS request as `item.speed` for Azure/ElevenLabs renders (Azure bakes it; ElevenLabs ignores it in practice).",
    "services/voice-config-service.cjs getEffectiveSpeed()/buildTTSConfig(): combines voice_config speed with a cadence multiplier and forwards it into the provider-specific TTS config (azure: voiceName+speed; elevenlabs: speed passed but unused downstream; xai: speed passed but provider has no such param).",
    "Under Tom's ruling these are now PLAYBACK/LEGACY metadata, not identity — the player renders belt-appropriate pace live (0.8x white / 0.9x yellow / 0.95x orange / 1.0x thereafter), so course_audio should be rendered at 1x going forward and voice_config's speed field should eventually be cleaned up / repurposed as a playback default rather than a render parameter."
  ],
